<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Requiem settings by Engarandus Juvenis (1490), Antoine Brumel (1516), Charpentier, Delalande, Mozart, Berlioz, Verdi, Britten and Stravinsky</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1490</span><span class="sg-chain-h">musical settings of the sequence</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Canons on the sequence (Giovanni Battista Martini)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">20 canons ending his set of 303</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphonie fantastique (Hector Berlioz)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Souvenirs, Op. 15 No. 3 &quot;Morte&quot; (Charles-Valentin Alkan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1837</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Prelude in A minor, Op. 28 No. 2 (Frédéric Chopin)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1839</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Totentanz (Franz Liszt)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1849</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Faust (Charles Gounod), act 4</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1859</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Songs and Dances of Death, No. 3 &quot;Trepak&quot; (Modest Mussorgsky)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1875</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Danse macabre; Symphony No. 3; Requiem (Camille Saint-Saëns)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1878 (the Requiem)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Manfred Symphony and other works (Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1872–1885</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 2 (Gustav Mahler)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1888–94</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Intermezzo, Op. 118 No. 6 (Johannes Brahms)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1893</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant melody quoted</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Book of Zephaniah 1:15–16 (Vulgate)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">main source of its imagery</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Book of Revelation, Matthew, 1 Thessalonians, 2 Peter and Luke</span><span class="sg-chain-h">further images</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Unetanneh Tokef (Jewish liturgy)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">appears to be related</span></li></ul></section>
